u2192 1453 | ~22883\u201323082 |\n| 1871 \u2192 632 | ~23083\u201323282 |\n| 1885 \u2192 749 | ~23283\u201323482 (latest) |\n\nThe unique static path is traversed in **exactly reverse chronological order**. 1460 received its only inbound contact ~800\u20131200 units *before* 1885 emitted its only event, so no influence could have flowed forward. Alternative routes are ruled out: 1885 has exactly one out-neighbour (749) and 1460 exactly one in-neighbour (632), each with a single event in the window.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_dc50ed4d\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1885, 749, 1453, 1871, 632, 1460],\n  \"window\": [21683, 24083],\n  \"confidence\": 0.88,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"support\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"A single static chain 1885->749->1453->1871->632->1460 connects the endpoints when time is ignored, but 100-unit binning of every node's events shows the hops fire in reverse chronological order: 632->1460 (~22283-22482) first, then 1453->1871, 749->1453, 1871->632, and finally 1885->749 (~23283-23482) last. The target is contacted long before the source ever acts, so no time-respecting, 600-unit-delay-bounded cascade exists. Confounder controls: 1885 and 1460 each have exactly one event and one partner in the window (steps 02-04), so the connectivity is not an artifact of hub popularity, and no alternate path can substitute; 1871's second in-neighbour 488 (step_08) does not lie downstream of 1885.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 29502, "total_output_tokens": 5813, "total_tokens": 35315, "total_latency_ms": 76417, "llm_calls": 7, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}